  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The idea is pretty simple:\n\nAllow avatars over 20k polygons but only if they include a <20k version to be shown on the low graphics setting.\nThis could also be expanded to other graphics settings. Example:\nlow: <10k\nmedium: <20k\nhigh: <40k\nUltra: no limit\n\nIn order to reduce the work an avatar creator has to do an automatic decimation function could be included in the SDK to automatically create a low, medium and high version!\n\nThis system can also be extended to textures, particles and other components.\nExamples:\n-Reducing the resolution of textures on lower end systems. (lower and mid res textures are generated when uploading and avatar)\n-Allowing the user to set a maximum numbers of particles that are being shown.\n-Allowing the users to enable or disable cameras / screens locally.\n-Allowing the user to locally disable dynamic / real-time light sources on avatars and objects.\n\n",
